Title: The Last Ferry
Credit: Adapted from a short story
Author: akuko test fixture

EXT. RIVER PIER - DUSK

MARA, thirties, a suitcase in one hand and a letter in the other, hurries onto the pier as the light fades.

OREN, sixties, coils the rope of a small ferry for the last crossing of the day.

OREN
We're closed.

She holds up the letter. He reads it, folds it away, and says nothing.

EXT. THE FERRY - MID-RIVER - NIGHT

The engine coughs and dies. Fog closes in around the little boat.

Oren kneels at the engine. Mara holds the lantern steady over his hands.

MARA
My sister lived over there.

Oren nods, not looking up.

EXT. FAR PIER - NIGHT

A WOMAN waits under a street lamp, her face hidden by the fog.

Mara steps off the ferry. Oren turns the boat back into the fog.

CUT TO:
